id: pm-web-hqqp
title: Investigate intermittent 2000-item graph latency failures in full coverage runs
description: "During the PR #173 review round, npm run release:check failed the unchanged 10000 ms large-corpus graph read assertion at 10959 ms. The same rebuilt package passed standalone linked graph acceptance at 2513 ms. The deterministic concurrent-create and external-writer consistency tests passed in the full npm run. Investigate instrumented-suite load and graph read cost without weakening the latency assertion or coverage thresholds; this measurement discrepancy is separate from the two requested review corrections."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-07T22:48:36.158Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-10T05:13:14.023Z"
author: codex-sol
acceptance_criteria: Explain and reproduce the full-suite latency discrepancy; retain the 10000 ms budget and repository coverage thresholds; record standalone and full npm/Bun graph receipts.
actual_result: "Combined full ordering reader10918ms rejected; public light reader ordering proven equal to full SDK scan, payloads remain certified with same lock and external-writer guard. Focused read5586ms,linked4639ms,final fullgate3230ms for2000items/2022nodes/23063relationships. Fixed10000ms limit retained; coverage files serial, operation-window timestamps, allsource inventory/thresholds unchanged. No capacity/deployment claim."
